{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Standardize the CLI write-command argument parsing: retire the hand-rolled manual loop for Python's stdlib argparse, WITHOUT changing observable behavior.\n\n## Context / Problem\nToday the CLI parses write-command args with a hand-rolled loop (src/rebar/_commands/claim.py _parse_force/_parse_assignee, and src/rebar/_commands/transition.py _parse_flags) carrying bespoke semantics not reflected in any schema: --assignee ABSENT is a None sentinel (=> ticket.default_assignee fallback) while explicit --assignee \"\" CLEARS the assignee. This is tech-debt: flags and --help can silently drift from actual behavior.\n\n## Dependency / sequencing\nDepends on blusterous-earthly-kitten, which normalizes the force surface (removes `force_close`, makes `transition`'s `--force[=<reason>]` a reason-carrying param matching `claim`, and drops the `--reason`-as-force-note fallback). This is a behavior-preserving MECHANICAL refactor that must preserve the POST-blusterous CLI surface, so it runs AFTER that semantic change to avoid re-encoding a soon-to-change flag and to avoid a conflicting edit on the same parser files.\n\n## Approach\nRefactor the CLI write-command parsing onto Python's stdlib argparse. argparse is the chosen default: zero new runtime dependency, portable, and it generates accurate --help; we do NOT adopt Click or Typer, to avoid adding a runtime dependency. This is a behavior-preserving ADAPTER REFACTOR, orthogonal to the parity oracle. Respect the module-size (<=800 LOC) and per-function complexity ratchets by extracting along existing call-graph seams rather than inflating a single function.\n\n## Contract preservation (must not regress, relative to the post-blusterous surface)\nFlag spellings, exit-code 10 (ConcurrencyError), the `--force[=<reason>]` reason-carrying bypass (bare `--force` -> \"(no reason given)\"; `--force=<reason>` -> that reason; `--reason` is NOT the force note), and the --assignee None-vs-empty-string distinction must be preserved exactly.\n\n## Scope\n- src/rebar/_commands/claim.py — replace the _parse_force/_parse_assignee hand loop with argparse, preserving the sentinel semantics.\n- src/rebar/_commands/transition.py — replace _parse_flags with argparse; same treatment.\n- Lib and MCP surfaces are OUT OF SCOPE (this is an adapter-local change).\n\n## Testing\n- Existing CLI interface tests pass unchanged (tests/interfaces).\n- `--force[=<reason>]` supplies the audit note inline (bare -> \"(no reason given)\"); `--reason` is admitted only as close_reason, never as the force note (test, consistent with blusterous).\n- --assignee absent => default_assignee fallback; --assignee \"\" => cleared (test asserts both).\n- A ConcurrencyError still exits 10.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] CLI write-command parsing goes through argparse and `--help` is generated (verified by running the command's --help and confirming it lists the flags).\n- [ ] The `--force[=<reason>]` reason-carrying form is preserved (bare -> \"(no reason given)\", `--force=<reason>` -> that reason); `--reason` is not repurposed as the force note (test).\n- [ ] The --assignee None-vs-empty-string distinction is preserved: absent => default_assignee fallback, \"\" => cleared (test asserts both).\n- [ ] Exit code 10 on ConcurrencyError is preserved (existing CLI interface tests pass).\n- [ ] `make lint` and `make typecheck` are green; module-size and complexity ratchets respected."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787089835802237001,"uuid":"62f48512-d273-421e-a960-8a2e4a6db700"}